"Statements I EXPECT, from reading source, not measured: `INSERT INTO \"aspect_memberships\" (\"aspect_id\", \"contact_id\", \"created_at\", \"updated_at\") VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)` under ActiveRecord::Base#save! (persisted contact, immediate through-insert), then within ActiveRecord::Base#save: `SELECT  1 AS one FROM \"contacts\" WHERE \"contacts\".\"person_id\" = ? AND \"contacts\".\"id\" != ? AND \"contacts\".\"user_id\" = ? LIMIT ?`, the blocks exists?, and `UPDATE \"contacts\" SET \"receiving\" = ?, \"updated_at\" = ? WHERE \"contacts\".\"id\" = ?` (column order is Rails'). After that, needs_dispatch is true, so the scenario will end in Redis::CannotConnectError before update_all, the same as scenario 1. That is acceptable because scenario 2 already carries update_all. "
